%erg 0.1
Title: Tighten erg ready "Equivalent to" help text for custom label vocabularies
Created: 2026-05-30
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-30T10:30Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

`erg ready`'s help text (and the generated `docs/erg-manual.md`) states it is
"Equivalent to `erg list open not blocked not needs-human not deferred`". But
`cmdReady` negates **every** label in `effectiveLabelSet(cfg)` — i.e. all
entries of `tickets/.ergrc [labels]`, not just the two defaults. Under a custom
`[labels]` vocabulary the stated equivalence is wrong/misleading.

Surfaced by Copilot on PR #192 (the Tag→Label rename, ticket 0175). The
imprecision is **pre-existing** — it predates the rename, which only changed
`tags`→`labels` in that sentence — so it was left out of 0175's scope.

## Relevant files
- `src/go/ready.go` — `helpReady` const (the "Equivalent to..." line) and
  `cmdReady` (the `effectiveLabelSet` negation loop).
- `docs/erg-manual.md` — generated from `erg --help --all`; regenerate via
  `make docs` after editing the help const, do not hand-edit.

## Actions
1. Reword the `helpReady` "Equivalent to..." sentence so it is accurate under
   any vocabulary, e.g. "Equivalent to `erg list open not blocked` with every
   configured label (`.ergrc [labels]`; default needs-human, deferred) also
   negated." Keep it concise.
2. `make docs` to regenerate `docs/erg-manual.md`.

## Test
- `tests/test_godoc.sh` or `tests/test_ready.sh`: assert the help text does NOT
  claim a fixed `not needs-human not deferred` equivalence (string check), so a
  future edit can't silently reintroduce the imprecise wording.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `helpReady` no longer asserts a default-only equivalence as if universal
- [ ] `docs/erg-manual.md` regenerated and consistent
- [ ] `make test` and `make validate` pass

## Notes
Cosmetic/doc-only — no behavior change to `cmdReady`.
